# There is no www-to-apex rule here, and adding one does not work. Cloudflare Pages
# ignores a source with a hostname in it: `https://www.wegowhen.com/* ... 301!` shipped
# to production on 2026-08-31 and https://www.wegowhen.com/faq still answered 200, not
# 301. The site is therefore live on both hostnames, held together by the
# `<link rel="canonical">` pointing at the apex that every page carries.
#
# The real fix is a zone-level Redirect Rule in the Cloudflare dashboard, which needs a
# credential this repo does not have. Do not re-add the line: an inert rule reads like
# a solved problem.

# The only path the prerenderer does not emit a file for. It rewrites to a shell whose
# `#root` is empty and whose head says `noindex`: baking the landing page's body in
# here would show the create-trip form to someone opening an invitation link, for as
# long as the JavaScript took to load.
#
# The target is written WITHOUT the `.html`, and that is not cosmetic. Pages serves
# `trip-shell.html` at `/trip-shell` and 308s `/trip-shell.html` to it, so a target
# spelled `/trip-shell.html` turns this 200 rewrite into a redirect: `/trip/abc123`
# answered 308 instead of serving the shell, which is every invitation link the product
# has ever issued. Measured against `wrangler pages dev` on 2026-08-31, both spellings.
/trip/*  /trip-shell  200

# Deliberately no `/* /index.html 200` catch-all. That answered every unknown path with
# a 200 and the home page's head - a soft 404 on an unlimited number of URLs. Pages now
# falls through to `dist/404.html`, which is a real 404 and carries `noindex`.
